  "term": "postherpetic neuralgia",
  "definition": "Postherpetic neuralgia is ongoing nerve pain that can remain after shingles-related rashes and blisters have healed, often affecting the facial skin. It results from activation of latent varicella-zoster virus and may follow herpes zoster involving the ear or eye.",
